Pandoc

Add Hugo Metadata at the Very Top:

Type your Hugo "Front Matter" on the first few lines of the document before your main text:

Plaintext
---
title: "Troubleshooting High-Pressure Hydraulics"
date: 2026-10-10
description: "Field guide for diagnosing relief valve pressure drops."
tags: ["Hydraulics", "Maintenance"]
---
Save Normally: Save your document as a standard .odt file inside a working folder (e.g., ~/Documents/drafts/hydraulics.odt).


To convert your document into a Hugo-compatible .md file, run pandoc in your terminal:

Bash
# General syntax:
pandoc -f odt -t markdown_strict+yaml_metadata_block input.odt -o output.md --extract-media=.

# Run this inside your Hugo site's content/ folder:
pandoc -f odt -t markdown_strict+yaml_metadata_block ~/Documents/drafts/hydraulics.odt \
  -o hydraulics.md \
  --extract-media=../static/images/

What this does: Pandoc extracts every image embedded in your LibreOffice file, dumps them directly into Hugo's /static/images/ folder, and automatically links them inside the generated Markdown file.
